GLYMUR DIAGNOSTIC (2026-07-30) — not for upstream, and not a fix.

Runtime knobs used to root-cause the suspend reset on the ASUS Zenbook A16
(UX3607OA, Snapdragon X2 Elite "glymur"). All default to 0, so a kernel built
with this patch behaves exactly like stock unless a knob is set.

  drivers/base/power/main.c
    glymur_pm_skip      bitmask, core_param  -> cmdline "glymur_pm_skip=N"
                          1 = skip suspend_device_irqs()/resume_device_irqs()
                          2 = skip dpm_noirq_suspend_devices()/resume
                          4 = skip dpm_suspend_late()/dpm_resume_early()
    glymur_pm_skip_bus  comma-separated bus names; skips the noirq suspend
                        callback for every device on those buses
    glymur_pm_skip_dev  comma-separated device-name PREFIXES (a PCI domain
                        prefix such as "0005:" also catches its :pcieNNN
                        port services)

  drivers/pci/pci-driver.c
    glymur_pci_skip     bitmask inside pci_pm_suspend_noirq()
                          1 = skip pci_prepare_to_sleep()  (stay in D0)
                          2 = skip pm->suspend_noirq()     (driver callback)
                          4 = skip pci_save_state()

WHAT THIS ESTABLISHED

  pm_test bisect: freezer and devices survive, platform resets the SoC.
  With s2idle, dpm_suspend_late()+dpm_suspend_noirq() is the whole window --
  the three platform_suspend_prepare* hooks are no-ops because s2idle_set_ops()
  is only ever called from drivers/acpi (x86).

  glymur_pm_skip=2 alone survives, so the fault is a per-device noirq callback.
  Bus and then device bisect narrows it to PCIe, and a single PCIe device
  performing its noirq suspend is sufficient to reset the SoC.

  Inside pci_pm_suspend_noirq(), skipping BOTH pci_save_state() and
  pci_prepare_to_sleep() (glymur_pci_skip=5) survives, while skipping either
  alone does not. Driver noirq callbacks are innocent.

  => PCI config-space access during dpm_suspend_noirq() resets this SoC, and
     the read and write paths are independently lethal.

  Reproduces identically on the bare upstream A16 device tree, with the GPU
  disabled, and with the WLAN PCIe branch physically removed. Not PME wakeup
  arming (already disabled), not D3cold, not any D-state change, and not the
  PCIe controller being runtime-suspended.

Symmetry note: every knob gates suspend and resume together. For the two skips
in device_suspend_noirq() no resume-side change is needed -- bailing there
leaves dev->power.is_noirq_suspended false, which device_resume_noirq() already
handles as its "suspend aborted in the noirq phase" case.

